          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/90374132737e5f3bd6a0b36e0ded662935552b61"
        }
      ],
      "message": "test: characterize buggy BIP-352 P2PKH extraction on malleated scriptSig\n\nAdd a unit test with a (third-party) malleated P2PKH scriptSig that\ncontains an OP_CHECKSIG with a bogus signature, followed by a\nconditional push of a wrong pubkey. In real validation the OP_CHECKSIG\nfails and the spend remains consensus-valid (which is verified in the\ntest as well), but since the scriptSig is evaluated with a dummy\nsignature checker that accepts any non-empty signature, the wrong\npubkey is extracted. Record this current (buggy) behavior; the test is\nupdated with the fix in the next commit.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Sebastian Falbesoner",
        "email": "sebastian.falbesoner@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-25T19:33:27Z"
      },
